zlib (1.4+ds1-1) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * zlib 1.4.
  * inflateGetDictionary() no longer writes more than 32 KiB on a stream
    that is reset after inflate() rejected its zlib header.
  * inflateBack() rejects distances that reach back too far. It no longer
    copies unwritten memory to the output.
  * Repeated deflatePrime() calls no longer write past the pending buffer.
  * inflate() no longer reads before its input after repeated
    inflatePrime() calls.
  * gzungetc() right after gzopen() no longer writes through an unset
    pointer.
  * gzsetparams() fails on a file opened with "T". It used unset deflate
    state.
  * deflateReset() drops the gzip header that deflateSetHeader() set.
  * inflateSync() finds a sync marker held in the bit buffer.
  * inflateSync() on a stream with windowBits 0 and no header yet sets a
    32 KiB window. A later zlib header no longer overruns a 1-byte window.
  * gzgets() with len 1 returns an empty string.
  * crc32_combine() and crc32_combine_op() use only the low 32 bits of the
    first CRC.
  * New functions: compress_z(), compress2_z(), compressBound_z(),
    deflateBound_z(), deflateUsed(), uncompress_z() and uncompress2_z().

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:11:21 +0000

